{
  "id": "ep049",
  "duration": 41.755,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.856,
      "text": "A dead star halfway to the Moon could erase your credit cards.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SGR 1806-20 108536main NeutronStar-Print1.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Conceptual Image Lab",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SGR_1806-20_108536main_NeutronStar-Print1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.033,
          "end": 3.867,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.856,
      "end": 10.001,
      "text": "This cosmic monster is a magnetar, an ultra-dense star only twenty kilometers wide.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Degenerate star sizes.png",
        "credit": "Grufo",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Degenerate_star_sizes.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.867,
          "end": 10.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.001,
      "end": 15.996,
      "text": "It generates a magnetic field of one thousand trillion gauss, the strongest in the universe.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Magnetar Fields.tif",
        "credit": "NASA's Goddard Space Flight Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magnetar_Fields.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.0,
          "end": 12.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 12.1,
          "end": 16.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.996,
      "end": 22.366,
      "text": "On December twenty-seventh, two thousand four, a starquake on one magnetar triggered a giant flare.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SGR 1806-20 108530main cloudballPrint.jpg",
        "credit": "U Harvard",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SGR_1806-20_108530main_cloudballPrint.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.0,
          "end": 19.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.133,
          "end": 22.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.366,
      "end": 28.911,
      "text": "In one-tenth of a second, the flare released more energy than our Sun emits in one hundred thousand years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gamma rays hitting the Earth's atmosphere.tif",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gamma_rays_hitting_the_Earth%27s_atmosphere.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.367,
          "end": 28.9,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.911,
      "end": 35.586,
      "text": "The blast traveled across the galaxy and briefly ionized and expanded Earth's upper atmosphere.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ISS-44 pass through Aurora australis.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Scott Kelly",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS-44_pass_through_Aurora_australis.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.9,
          "end": 32.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.833,
          "end": 35.6,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.586,
      "end": 41.405,
      "text": "That same magnetic fury is why a dead star halfway to the Moon could erase your credit cards.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SGR 1806-20 108536main NeutronStar-Print1.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Conceptual Image Lab",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SGR_1806-20_108536main_NeutronStar-Print1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.6,
          "end": 41.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
